The madvise ioctl (`xe_vm_madvise_ioctl`) lacked validation to reject PAT indices with `XE_COH_NONE` coherency mode when applied to CPU cached memory. This allowed userspace to set a non-coherent access pattern on CPU cached buffers, which on integrated GPUs causes GPU reads to bypass CPU caches and directly access DRAM, potentially leaking stale sensitive data from previously freed pages.

